  "description": "Total face value of Australian Federal Government debt on issue in billions of dollars. Unlike net debt, this does not subtract government financial assets held against the borrowings.",
  "explainer": "Gross debt is the total amount the government has borrowed \u2014 the face value of all Commonwealth Government Securities (bonds) on issue, managed by the Australian Office of Financial Management. It only goes up in dollar terms, making it more alarming-looking than net debt but less analytically meaningful without context. Australia crossed $1 trillion in gross debt for the first time in 2023. Compare with net debt as % of GDP for a more accurate picture of fiscal position \u2014 at around 22% of GDP, Australia remains low by international standards despite the large absolute number.",
